    "notes": "UNBLOCKED 3 October 2026. The collector (1.2.0) now samples tomcat.threads.busy and tomcat.threads.config.max as mid-run gauges, so threads_busy_peak_threads and threads_config_max_threads travel in every snapshot. The fixture is ready to capture against a 1.2.0 collector.\nThe distinguishing evidence is specific and small: with four request threads, requests queue BEFORE they ever reach the datasource, so pending_peak_connections stays near zero and acquire_mean_ms stays tiny while threads_busy_peak_threads is pinned at 4 (100% utilisation) and p99 is dreadful. That combination -- terrible latency, healthy-looking pool, saturated thread counter -- is what separates thread saturation from pool exhaustion.\nPREVIOUSLY BLOCKED: The gap was documented in docs/ref/DEBT.md. The thread metrics existed in the profile's metric_map but not in snapshot_metrics or gauges, so snapshots carried no thread fields and capturing would have baked the absence in for all replay built on it.\n"
